-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  std_raylib_ext_linux.pcpp - std compliance: the raylib_ext unit

  `import raylib_ext;` gives raylib's file loaders an IO form. Every IO form
  is compared with raylib's own file-name form on a real file of the same
  bytes (written beside this program, removed after): what the file-name
  form gives, the IO form gives.

  Data: LoadFileDataIO and LoadFileTextIO over a memory IO (bytes with a NUL
  and a CRLF in them), a file IO and a zip entry (std_customio_stored.zip:
  data/bytes.bin, hello.txt); an empty IO as an empty file; a failing IO,
  and nil, as a missing file (nil, size 0). Every result is unloaded with
  UnloadFileData / UnloadFileText.

  Each row prints ok or FAIL with its name; the last is `done <failures>`.
  raylib's own log is off (SetTraceLogLevel(LOG_NONE)), so the output is the
  rows alone.

  The Linux half of std_raylib_ext: the same program, the Linux
  expectations.
*******************************************************************************/

